PATCH 187 -- rebase the MGAVIDEO pitch-cache MRU list walk/unlink FUN_0000_02c1 onto DGROUP near
offsets (the NEXT FRONTIER from patches 185/186: the mission-viewport rowtable-pitch method reached
via c55c from the first 22dd command handler FUN_0000_2322).

FUN_0000_02c1 (mga, asm 0x02c1-0x02f4 in re_out/fist_mga_image.bin) caches a per-pitch scanline
rowtable in an MRU linked list.  The driver runs DS=ES=DGROUP (0x1c00); the list head is the WORD at
DGROUP:0x798 and every node lives at a DGROUP NEAR OFFSET with fields [+0]=next-link, [+2]=pitch,
[+4]=rowtable-offset.  asm:

    2d0: mov bx,0x798        ; bx = head slot addr
    2d3: mov dx,[bx]         ; dx = link          (LOOP TOP)
    2d5: or dx,dx / je 0x2f5 ; empty/tail -> build
    2d9: mov si,bx / mov bx,dx
    2dd: cmp [bx+2],ax / jne 0x2d3   ; pitch match? else loop
    2e2: mov ax,[bx] / mov [si],ax   ; unlink cur (prev->next = cur->next)
    2e6: mov ax,bx / xchg ax,[0x798] / mov [bx],ax   ; move cur to head
    2ee: mov ax,[bx+4] / mov [0x794],ax              ; publish rowtable offset
    2f5: mov [bx+2],ax ; mov di,[bx+4] ; stos ax x2 loop 0x64 ; jmp 2e2  ; build 200 WORD entries

Patch 119 fixed ONLY the per-pitch BUILD stos loop (the `piVar6 = (int*)puVar4[2]` int-stride bug),
NOT the walk/unlink: Ghidra typed the list links as host pointers (`puVar5 = *puVar4`; `param_2`,
`puVar5` = raw near offsets, e.g. param_2=0x66ac) so `*param_2 = *puVar5` wild-dereferenced ->
SIGSEGV (build/fist_mga.c LAB_0000_02e2).  The menu returns early at pitch 0x140 (the list is never
walked there); the mission viewport uses a non-0x140 pitch, so the walk runs on the ACCEPT cascade.

This rewrites the whole walk + unlink + move-to-front + build as a faithful transliteration in the
DGROUP-offset model, tracking `prev` (si) and `cur` (bx) as uint16_t near offsets and rebasing every
node/head access onto g_mem+0x1c000.  Field offsets, the move-to-front xchg, and the build stos loop
are instruction-faithful.  `param_2` (a Ghidra-spurious 2nd register input, immediately overwritten
by the walk) is unused.  Behaviour-neutral for the 19 verify flows: 02c1 returns at the 0x140 early
exit on the menu path (the walk/build below is unreachable there); the pre-patch wild deref would
already SIGSEGV any flow that reached it.

